				<guid>http://localhost:1313/everyday-data/privacy/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Last updated: July 22, 2026&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your privacy matters.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Everyday Data is an independent educational and research project. This website is designed to collect as little personal information as possible.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;information-we-collect&#34;&gt;Information We Collect&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This website does not require user accounts. It does not intentionally collect personal information from visitors unless they voluntarily subscribe to Everyday Data updates.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you contact me through LinkedIn or GitHub, your information is handled according to the privacy policies of those platforms.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>About Everyday Data</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/everyday-data/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/everyday-data/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;turning-curiosity-into-research&#34;&gt;Turning curiosity into research&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I wanted to move beyond simply wondering&amp;hellip; I wanted to know.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;How much water could actually be saved?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;How much waste could be avoided?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;What is the environmental impact of a particular everyday choice?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;What does the data actually tell us?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Everyday Data is my personal space for exploring those questions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I use publicly available data, scientific literature, transparent calculations, and visualizations to investigate everyday choices and put them into a context that is easier to understand.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
